// Policy 2 of 7 -- "Output-to-input integrity".
// From "Securing AI agents with temporal policies in Amazon Bedrock AgentCore", AWS Machine
// Learning Blog, 06 AUG 2026. The policy below is the article's listing VERBATIM, copied byte
// for byte from the published page on 2026-10-02 (reference/README.md has the provenance).
//
// THE ARTICLE'S STATED INTENT:
//   The portfolio_id passed to execute_trade must exactly match one of the portfolio IDs
//   returned by get_client_profile. The agent cannot fabricate or substitute a different
//   portfolio ID.
//
// NOTE what the policy compares: the trade's `input.profile_id` against an earlier
// get_client_profile's `input.profile_id` -- what that call was ASKED for, not what it RETURNED,
// and a profile id, not a portfolio id. See README.md, finding 3.

permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 24h (
        AgentCore::Action::"get_client_profile"::response{
            input.profile_id: context.input.profile_id,
            eventResource: resource
        }
    )
};
